    "Transience is loss over time (A-III). Absent-mindedness is a lapse of attention, so the information was never well encoded (B-IV). Blocking is temporary inaccessibility, as in tip-of-the-tongue (C-I). Misattribution is assigning a memory to the wrong source (D-II). A-III, B-I, C-IV, D-II swaps absent-mindedness and blocking. A-IV, B-III, C-I, D-II swaps transience and absent-mindedness. A-III, B-IV, C-II, D-I swaps blocking and misattribution.",
